Z||000000||fierocrazy||09-06-2000||09:53 PM||||i hate to go into to much detail, there isnt a thing that isnt brand new on this car. I did the 3.2 conversion myself so I am no dummy.  So through the questions at me but I can give you some background:  <BR>My problem is the car barely idles, but runs strong once it gets going, the only code is 32, which is EGR which i made a plate and got rid of the EGR valve..but everything esle to the EGR is there, but that shouldn't effect the idle. the only other thing that doesnt work is the tach ( i lost my tach filter, opps )<BR>now the good stuff<BR>    Igintion :GM MSD blaster, 8mm wires, Napa cap and rotor, platium plugs<BR>     Fuel system: Corvette fuel pump, AN #6 feed line, Russel clear fuel filter, Accel variable fuel regulator ( 36 lbs key on, 30 lbs. at idle) GM 3.8 injectors<BR>     Short block: 2.8 block ( .010 off deck surface) 3.1 crank, camaro steal head hyper pistons ( i think about 9 to 1 compression)<BR>     Heads: pocket ported, resurfaced .010 , 90 lbs on springs, the rest is stock<BR>     I replaced the Idle control vavle and replaced all the intake gaskets a week ago, checked all the vacuem lines, it all seems the be ok.. the plugs are white aroung the eletrobe and carbon on the treads which looks ok to me too...<BR>  Any suggestions or questions would be appeciated I am all out of ideas.. thanks<P>85GT 3.2||||reg||1
